{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Summable"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.ladder_lt_of_sum_bound_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.ladder_lt_of_sum_bound_exp","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderUniformBound.lean#L233-L261","doc":"**The ladder exclusion via Mathlib's product bound** — an independent route\nto `ladder_lt_of_sum_bound`, with no `S < 1` hypothesis and no sign hypothesis\non the rungs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.sum_bound_of_ladder_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.sum_bound_of_ladder_ge","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderUniformBound.lean#L210-L219","doc":"The contrapositive an agent actually wants: a ladder that DOES reach `F`\nforces a total absolute rung weight above `S`.  Reading the corpus numbers into\nit is the probe's job, not this file's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.ladder_lt_of_sum_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.ladder_lt_of_sum_bound","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderUniformBound.lean#L179-L208","doc":"**The sign-independent ladder exclusion.**  With the cosine cap and a\nuniform bound `S` on the total absolute rung weight, the ladder is strictly\nbelow any requirement `F` with `1 < F · (1 - S)` — equivalently `F > 1/(1-S)`\n— for rungs of **either sign**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.sum_abs_le_of_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.sum_abs_le_of_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderUniformBound.lean#L154-L177","doc":"If every term is bounded by `C` times a non-negative weight, and the\nweights total at most `G`, the terms total at most `C * G`.  This is what turns\n\"every coefficient is `O(1)`\" into a single checkable scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.prod_one_add_mul_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.prod_one_add_mul_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderUniformBound.lean#L127-L152","doc":"**Weierstrass product bound, division-free form.**  A finite product\n`∏(1 + xᵢ)` whose terms have total absolute weight `S < 1` satisfies\n`∏(1 + xᵢ) · (1 - S) ≤ 1`.  No sign hypothesis on the `xᵢ`, and no division\nanywhere — the `1/(1-S)` reading is the immediate consequence and is stated in\nthe docstring of `ladder_lt_of_sum_bound` rather than in a type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.prod_one_add_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.prod_one_add_pos","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderUniformBound.lean#L107-L125","doc":"With total absolute weight below 1, every factor `1 + xᵢ` is positive, so\nthe product is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.sum_abs_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderUniformBound.sum_abs_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderUniformBound.lean#L100-L105","doc":"The total absolute weight of a list is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0}]}